{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791548520,"nonce":"NMSvI6RElixcY/IIsqikFlrCi+s=","message":"Further macOS TreeMotion memory check after AIR and GC improvements: application Auto and pinned Cranelift produce indistinguishable sampled pixels and similar replay timing/footprint (about 130 MiB in this particular run). Auto promotes three functions to LLVM; Cranelift promotes none.\n\nSource finding: crates/ash_interp/src/tiering.rs::tiered_compile_tier_inner calls start_deferred_llvm(ctx) unconditionally, including TierMode::Cranelift. This mode therefore still creates the deferred LLVM module on its first Cranelift promotion. Disabling actual LLVM promotions alone is not a measurement of an LLVM-free process. The required follow-up is to skip the deferred builder when LLVM is unreachable by the chosen ladder, and verify reload/compiled-only behavior and the pinned-mode memory difference. No ladder policy or threshold changed in this GC/atlas milestone.\n\nEvidence: Ashui .ashui/memory-comparison/idle-llvm-131635/report.json. This does not establish LLVM as the dominant remaining physical-footprint owner; decoded bytecode and retained AIR still contribute ~14.5 and ~12.2 MiB of live malloc, separate from GC and GPU mappings.","files":null}]}